10.8:
He sits in the hiding places of the villages; 
In the secret places he murders the innocent; 
His eyes are on the lookout for the helpless.

10.9:
He lies in wait in a secret place, as a lion in his den; 
He lies in wait to catch the poor; 
He catches the poor, drawing him into his net.

100.3:
Know that 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, He is Elohim; 
He has made us, and we are His - 
His people and the sheep of His pasture.

100.5:
For 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 is good; 
His kindness is everlasting, 
And His truth, to all generations.

101.3:
I put no matter of Beliya’al before my eyes; 
I hate the work of those who fall away; 
It does not cling to me.

101.5:
Him who secretly slanders his neighbor I cut off; 
I do not tolerate one 
Who has a haughty look and a proud heart.

102.2:
Do not hide Your face from me 
In the day of my distress; 
Incline Your ear to me; 
In the day I call, answer me speedily.

102.10:
Because of Your displeasure and Your wrath; 
For You have lifted me up 
And thrown me down.

102.19:
For He looked down 
From the height of His qodesh place; 
From the shamayim 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 viewed the earth,

102.24:
I said, “O my Ĕl, 
Do not take me away in the midst of my days; 
Your years are throughout all generations.

102.26:
“They shall perish, but You remain; 
And all of them grow old like a garment; 
You change them like a coat, 
And they are changed.

104.8:
They go up the mountains; 
They go down the valleys, 
To the place which You founded for them.

106.7:
Our fathers in Mitsrayim did not understand Your wonders; 
They did not remember Your many kindnesses, 
But rebelled by the sea, the Sea of Reeds.

106.9:
And He rebuked the Sea of Reeds, and it dried up; 
And He led them through the depths, 
Through a wilderness.

106.43:
Many times He delivered them; 
But they rebelled in their plans, 
So they were brought low for their wickedness.

107.26:
They go up to the shamayim, 
They go down to the depths; 
Their being is melted because of evil.

107.38:
And He baraḵ them, 
And they increase greatly; 
And He does not let their cattle diminish.

109.16:
Because he did not remember to show kindness, 
But persecuted the poor and needy man; 
And the broken-hearted, to put to death.

109.21:
But You, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, Aḏonai, 
Deal with me for Your Name’s sake; 
Because Your kindness is good, deliver me.

11.1:
To the chief singer. Of Dawiḏ. In 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 I have taken refuge; 
Why do you say to me, 
“Flee to your mountain like a bird”?

11.7:
For 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 is righteous, 
He has loved righteousness; 
The upright shall see His face.

112.10:
ר,𐤓 The wicked sees it and shall be wroth;
שׁ,𐤔 He gnashes his teeth and shall melt.
ת,𐤕 The desire of the wicked perish.

115.7:
They have hands, but they do not handle; 
They have feet, but they do not walk; 
They make no sound through their throat.

115.12:
𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 has remembered us; 
He baraḵ us; 
He baraḵ the house of Yisra’ĕl; 
He baraḵ the house of Aharon.

116.3:
The cords of death were around me, 
And the pains of the grave came upon me; 
I found distress and sorrow.

116.16:
O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, I am truly Your servant, 
I am Your servant, the son of Your female servant; 
You have loosed my bonds.

118.11:
They surrounded me, 
Even they surrounded me; 
In the Name of 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 shall I cut them off.

118.12:
They surrounded me like bees; 
They were extinguished like burning thorns; 
In the Name of 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 I shall cut them off.

118.15:
The voice of rejoicing and deliverance 
Is in the tents of the righteous; 
The right hand of 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 is doing mightily.

118.27:
𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 is Ĕl, and He gave us light; 
Bind the festal offering 
With cords to the horns of the altar.

119.43:
And do not take away from my mouth 
The Word of truth entirely, 
For I have waited for Your Right- Rulings;

119.48:
That I might lift up my hands to Your Commands, 
Which I have loved; 
While I meditate on Your Laws.

119.70:
Their heart has become like fat, 
Without feeling; 
I have delighted in Your Torah.

119.78:
Let the proud be put to shame, 
For with lies they perverted me; 
I study Your Orders.

119.86:
All Your Commands are trustworthy; 
They have persecuted me with lies; 
Help me!

119.119:
You have made to cease 
All the wicked of the earth, like dross; 
Therefore I have loved Your Witnesses.

119.145:
ק,𐤒 I have called with all my heart; 
Answer me, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄! 
I observe Your Laws.

119.176:
I have strayed like a lost sheep; 
Seek Your servant, 
For I have not forgotten Your Commands.

12.4:
Who said, “With our tongue we do mightily; 
Our lips are our own; 
Who is master over us?”

124.7:
Our being has escaped like a bird 
From the snare of the trappers; 
The snare was broken, and we have escaped.

127.2:
In vain do you rise up early, 
To sit up late, to eat the bread of toil; 
So He gives His beloved sleep.

129.8:
And those who pass by shall not say, 
“The beraḵah of 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 be upon you; 
We have baraḵ you in the Name of 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄!”

130.7:
O Yisra’ĕl, wait for 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄; 
For with 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 there is kindness. 
And with Him is much redemption,

132.11:
𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 has sworn in truth to Dawiḏ; 
He does not turn from it, 
“Of the fruit of your body I place upon your throne.

135.7:
Causing vapors to go up 
From the ends of the earth; 
He made lightning for the rain, 
Bringing forth wind from His treasuries;

135.9:
He sent signs and wonders 
Into your midst, O Mitsrayim, 
On Pharaoh and on all his servants;

138.2:
I bow myself toward Your qodesh Hĕyḵal, 
And give thanks to Your Name; 
For Your kindness and for Your truth; 
For You have made great Your Word, 
Your Name, above all.

138.6:
Though 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 is exalted, 
He looks on the humble; 
But the proud He perceives from a distance.

139.18:
If I should count them, 
They would be more than the sand; 
When I wake up, I am still with You.

14.3:
They have all turned aside, they have together become filthy; 
No one is doing good, 
Not even one.

140.4:
Guard me, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, from the hands of the wicked; 
Guard me from a man of violence, 
Who have schemed to trip up my steps.

140.5:
The proud have hidden a trap for me, and cords; 
They have spread a net by the wayside; 
They have laid snares for me. Selah.

140.10:
“Let burning coals fall on them; 
Let them be made to fall into the fire, 
Into deep pits, let them not rise again.

141.8:
But my eyes are upon You, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 Aḏonai. 
In You I take refuge; 
Do not pour out my life.

142.4:
Look to the right hand and see, 
And no one is concerned for me; 
No refuge remains to me; 
No one inquires after my being.

143.3:
For the enemy has pursued my being; 
He has crushed my life to the ground; 
He has made me dwell in dark places, 
Like the dead of old.

143.5:
I remembered the days of old; 
I meditated on all Your works; 
I ponder on the work of Your hands.

144.1:
Of Dawiḏ. Baruḵ be 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 my Rock, 
Who is teaching my hands for fighting, 
My fingers for battle;

144.7:
Send forth Your hand from above; 
Rescue me and deliver me out of great waters, 
From the hand of foreigners,

144.11:
Rescue me and deliver me from the hand of foreigners, 
Whose mouth has spoken falsehood, 
And whose right hand is a right hand of lies;

144.12:
Because our sons are like plants 
Grown up in their youth; 
Our daughters like hewn stones, 
Polished, like a palace building;

144.13:
Let our storehouses be filled, 
Supplying all kinds; 
Let our sheep bring forth thousands 
And ten thousands in our fields;

144.14:
Our cattle well-laden; 
No breaking in, no going out; 
And no crying in our streets.

147.20:
He has not done so with any nation; 
And they have not known Right-Rulings! 
Hallelu-Yah!

149.9:
To execute on them the written Right-Ruling; 
A splendor it is for all His kind ones. 
Hallelu-Yah!

15.3:
He has not slandered with his tongue, 
He has not done evil to his neighbor, 
Nor lifted up a reproach against his friend;

15.4:
In whose eyes a reprobate one is despised, 
But he esteems those who revere 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄; 
He who swears to his own hurt and does not change;

16.4:
The sorrows of those who run after another one are increased; 
I would not pour out their drink offerings of blood, 
Nor take up their names on my lips.

16.11:
You show me the path of ḥai; 
In Your presence is joy to satisfaction; 
At Your right hand are pleasures forever.

17.3:
You have examined my heart; 
You have visited me in the night; 
You have tried me - You find I have not schemed; 
My mouth would not transgress.

18.2:
𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 is my rock and my stronghold and my deliverer; 
My Ĕl is my rock, I take refuge in Him; 
My shield and the horn of my deliverance, my high tower.

18.7:
And the earth shook and trembled; 
Even the foundations of the mountains were troubled 
And they shook, because He was wroth.

18.8:
Smoke went up from His nostrils, 
And consuming fire from His mouth; 
Coals were kindled by it.

18.11:
He made darkness His covering; 
Around Him His booth, 
Darkness of waters, thick clouds of the skies.

18.30:
The Ĕl - His Way is perfect; 
The Word of 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 is proven; 
He is a shield to all who take refuge in Him.

18.35:
And You give me the shield of Your deliverance; 
And Your right hand supports me, 
And Your lowliness makes me great.

18.43:
You deliver me from the strivings of the people, 
You put me at the head of the nations; 
A people I have not known serve me.

18.48:
My deliverer from my enemies. 
You lift me up above those who rise against me; 
You deliver me from a man of violence.

19.6:
Its rising is from one end of the shamayim, 
And its circuit to the other end; 
And naught is hidden from its heat.

19.9:
The reverence of 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 is clean, standing forever; 
The Right-Rulings of 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 are true, 
They are righteous altogether,

19.10:
More desirable than gold,
Than much fine gold; 
And sweeter than honey and the honeycomb.

20.6:
Now I know that 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 shall save His anointed; 
He answers him from His qodesh shamayim 
With the saving might of His right hand.

21.9:
You make them as a furnace of fire in the time of Your presence; 
𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 swallows them up in His wrath, 
And fire consumes them.

22.11:
Do not be far from Me, 
For distress is near; 
For there is none to help.

22.14:
I have been poured out like water, 
And all My bones have been spread apart; 
My heart has become like wax; 
It has melted in the midst of My inward parts.

22.15:
My strength is dried like a potsherd, 
And My tongue is cleaving to My jaws; 
And to the dust of death You are appointing Me.

22.16:
For dogs have surrounded Me; 
A crowd of evil ones have encircled Me, 
Piercing My hands and My feet;

22.24:
For He has not despised
 Nor hated the affliction of the afflicted; 
Nor has He hidden His face from Him; 
But when He cried to Him, He heard.

22.26:
The meek ones eat and are satisfied; 
Let those who seek Him hallelu𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄. 
Let your heart live forever!

23.3:
He turns back my being; 
He leads me in paths of righteousness 
For His Name’s sake.

23.5:
You spread before me a table in the face of my enemies; 
You have anointed my head with oil; 
My cup runs over.

25.2:
ב,𐤁 O my Elohim, in You I have put my trust; 
Let me not be ashamed; 
Let not my enemies exult over me.

25.7:
ח,𐤇 Do not remember the sins of my youth, and my transgressions;
According to Your kindness remember me, 
For Your goodness’ sake, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄.

27.1:
Of Dawiḏ. 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 is my light and my deliverance; 
Whom should I fear? 
𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 is the refuge of my life; 
Whom should I dread?

27.5:
For in the day of evil He hides me in His booth; 
In the covering of His Tent He hides me; 
On a rock He raises me up.

27.6:
And now my head is lifted up above my enemies all around me; 
And I offer in His Tent with offerings of shouts; 
I sing, I sing praises to 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄.

27.9:
Do not hide Your face from me; 
Do not turn Your servant away in displeasure; 
You have been my help; 
Do not leave me nor forsake me, 
O Elohim of my deliverance.

28.4:
Give to them according to their deeds, 
And according to the evil of their practices; 
Give to them according to the work of their hands; 
Bring back to them what they deserve.

28.7:
𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 is my strength, and my shield; 
My heart has trusted in Him, and I have been helped; 
Therefore my heart exults, 
And with my song I thank Him.

29.3:
The voice of 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 is over the waters; 
The Ĕl of esteem thunders; 
𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 is over many waters.

29.9:
The voice of 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 makes the deer give birth, 
And strips the forests bare; 
And in His Hĕyḵal everyone says, “Esteem!”

3.7:
Arise, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄; 
Save me, O my Elohim! 
Because You have smitten all my enemies on the cheek; 
You have broken the teeth of the wicked.

30.7:
𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, in Your good pleasure 
You have made my mountain to stand strong; 
You hid Your face, and I was troubled.

31.1:
In You, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, I have taken refuge; 
Let me never be ashamed; 
Deliver me in Your righteousness.

31.7:
I exult and rejoice in Your kindness, 
For You have seen my affliction; 
You have known the distresses of my life,

31.13:
For I hear the evil report of many; 
Fear is from all around; 
When they take counsel together against me, 
They plot to take away my life.

31.15:
My times are in Your hand; 
Deliver me from the hand of my enemies, 
And from those who pursue me.

31.17:
Do not let me be ashamed, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, 
For I have called upon You; 
Let the wicked be ashamed; 
Let them be silenced in the grave.

31.20:
In the secrecy of Your presence 
You shall hide them from the plots of man; 
You shelter them in a booth from the strife of tongues.

32.7:
You are my hiding place; 
You preserve me from distress; 
You surround me with songs of deliverance. Selah.

32.8:
“Let Me instruct you and teach you in the Way you should go;
Let Me counsel,
My eye be on you.

32.10:
Many are the sorrows of the wicked; 
But as for the one trusting in 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, 
Kindness surrounds him.

35.8:
Let ruin come upon him unawares, 
And let his net that he hid catch himself; 
Let him fall in it, into ruin.

35.13:
But I, when they were sick, I put on sackcloth; 
I humbled my being with fastings; 
And my prayer would return to my own bosom.

35.15:
But they rejoiced at my stumbling 
And gathered together; 
The smiters gathered against me, 
And I did not know it; 
They tore in pieces without ceasing,

35.22:
This You have seen, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄; 
Do not be silent. 
O Aḏonai, do not be far from me.

35.24:
Rule me rightly, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 my Elohim, 
According to Your righteousness; 
And let them not rejoice over me.

36.4:
He plots wickedness on his bed; 
He places himself in a way that is not good; 
He does not despise evil.

36.6:
Your righteousness is like the mighty mountains; 
Your Right-Rulings are a great deep; 
O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, You save man and beast.

36.12:
There the workers of wickedness have fallen; 
They have been overthrown 
And have been unable to rise.

37.7:
ד,𐤃 Rest in 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, and wait patiently for Him; 
Do not fret because of him who prospers in his way, 
Because of the man doing wicked devices.

37.9:
For evil-doers are cut off; 
But those who wait on 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, 
They shall inherit the earth.

37.10:
ו,𐤅 Yet a little while and the wicked one is no more; 
And you shall look on his place, 
But it is not.

37.25:
נ,𐤍 I have been young, and now I am old; 
Yet I have not seen the righteous forsaken, 
Or his seed begging bread.

37.40:
And 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 helps them and delivers them; 
He delivers them from the wicked and saves them, 
Because they took refuge in Him.

38.6:
I have been bent down; 
I have been bowed down very much; 
All day long I have gone mourning.

38.12:
And those seeking my life lay a snare; 
And those seeking my evil have spoken of destruction, 
And utter deceit all day long.

38.19:
But my enemies are alive; 
They have become strong; 
And those hating me falsely are many.

39.2:
I became dumb, keeping still; 
I was silent, from good; 
And my pain was stirred.

39.3:
My heart was hot within me; 
While I was meditating, the fire burned. 
Then I spoke with my tongue:

39.5:
“See, You have made my days as handbreadths, 
And my lifetime is as naught before You; 
Only, all men standing, are all breath. Selah.

39.6:
“As but a shadow each one walks; 
They busy themselves, only in vain; 
He heaps up, 
But knows not who gathers them.

39.11:
“When You chastise man for wickedness with reproofs, 
You consume what he loves, like a moth; 
All men are but a breath. Selah.

39.12:
“Hear my prayer, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, 
And give ear to my cry; 
Do not be silent at my tears; 
For I am a stranger with You, 
A sojourner, as all my fathers were.

4.1:
Answer me when I call, O Elohim of my righteousness! 
You gave relief to me when I was in distress; 
Show favor to me, and hear my prayer.

40.3:
Then He put a new song in my mouth; 
Praise to our Elohim; 
Many see and revere, 
And trust in 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄.

40.5:
O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 my Elohim, many are the wonders 
Which You have done, and Your purposes toward us; 
There is no one to compare with You; 
I declare and speak: 
They are too many to be numbered.

40.6:
Slaughtering and meal offering You did not desire? 
But a body You have prepared for Me; 
Burnt offering and sin offering You did not ask for?

40.9:
I have proclaimed the Good News of righteousness, 
In the great assembly; 
See, I do not restrain my lips, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, You know.

40.10:
I did not conceal Your righteousness within my heart; 
I have declared Your trustworthiness and Your deliverance; 
I did not hide Your kindness and Your truth 
From the great assembly.

40.12:
For evils without number have surrounded me; 
My wickednesses have overtaken me, 
And I have been unable to see; 
They became more than the hairs of my head; 
And my heart has failed me.

40.17:
But I am poor and needy; 
Let Aḏonai think upon me. 
You are my help and my deliverer; 
O my Elohim, do not delay!

41.4:
As for me, I said, 
“O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, show me favor; 
Heal me, for I have sinned against You.”

41.6:
And when one comes to visit, he speaks falsely; 
His heart gathers wickedness to itself; 
He goes out, he speaks of it.

42.8:
By day 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 commands His kindness, 
And by night His song is with me; 
A prayer to the Ĕl of my ḥai.

44.17:
All this has come upon us; 
But we have not forgotten You, 
Neither have we been false to Your Covenant.

45.1:
My heart is overflowing with a good word; 
I address my works to the Meleḵ; 
My tongue is the pen of a speedy writer.

45.2:
You are more handsome than the sons of men; 
Favor has been poured upon Your lips; 
Therefore Elohim has baraḵ You forever.

45.4:
And ride prosperously in Your splendor, 
On the matter of truth and humility, righteousness; 
And let Your right hand make known reverence.

45.6:
Your throne, O Elohim, is forever and ever; 
The sceptre of Your Malḵuth 
Is a sceptre of straightness.

45.7:
You have loved righteousness and hated wickedness; 
Therefore Elohim, Your Elohim, has anointed You 
With the oil of gladness more than Your companions.

45.8:
All Your garments are myrrh and aloes, cassia; 
Out of the palaces of ivory, 
Stringed instruments have made You glad.

45.10:
Listen, O daughter, and see, 
And incline your ear, 
And forget your own people and your father’s house;

45.13:
The daughter of the Meleḵ 
Is all esteemed within; 
Her dress is embroidered with gold.

45.14:
She is brought to the Meleḵ in embroidered work; 
Maidens, her companions following her, 
Are brought to You.

46.10:
Be still, and know that I am Elohim; 
I am exalted among nations, 
I am exalted in the earth!

48.10:
According to Your Name, O Elohim, 
So is Your praise to the ends of the earth; 
Your right hand is filled with righteousness.

48.12:
Walk about Tsiyon, 
And go all around her. 
Count her towers;

48.13:
Apply your heart to her rampart; 
Go through her citadels; 
So that you report it to the coming generation.

49.11:
Their graves are their houses, forever; 
Their dwelling places, to all generations; 
They call lands after their own names.

49.14:
Like sheep they shall be laid in the grave; 
Death shall shepherd them; 
And the upright rule over them in the morning; 
And their form is consumed in the grave, 
Far from their dwelling.

5.7:
But I, I enter Your house 
In the greatness of Your kindness; 
I bow myself toward Your qodesh Hĕyḵal in Your reverence.

5.9:
For there is no stability in their mouth; 
Their inward part is destruction; 
Their throat is an open grave; 
They flatter with their tongue.

5.11:
But let all who take refuge in You rejoice; 
Let them ever shout for joy, because You shelter them; 
And let those who love Your Name exult in You.

50.21:
“You have done this, and I kept silent; 
You have thought that I was altogether like you - 
I rebuke you, and put it in order before your eyes.

50.23:
“Whoever offers praise esteems Me; 
And to him who prepares a way, 
I show the deliverance of Elohim.”

51.4:
Against You, You alone, have I sinned, 
And done evil in Your eyes; 
That You might be proven right in Your words; 
Be clear when You judge.

51.19:
Then You would delight in slaughterings of righteousness, 
In burnt offering and complete burnt offering; 
Then young bulls would be offered on Your altar.

53.3:
They have all turned aside; 
They have together become filthy; 
No one is doing good, not even one.

54.3:
For strangers have risen up against me, 
And cruel men have sought after my life; 
They have not put Elohim before them. Selah.

55.15:
Let death come upon them; 
Let them go down into the grave alive, 
For evil is in their dwellings, in their midst.

55.20:
He has put forth his hands against those 
Who were at peace with him; 
He has broken his Covenant.

55.22:
Cast your burden on 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, 
And let Him sustain you; 
He never allows the righteous to be shaken.

55.23:
For You, O Elohim, bring them down 
To the pit of destruction; 
Men of blood and deceit do not reach half their days; 
But I, I trust in You.

56.1:
Show me favor, O Elohim, 
For man would swallow me up; 
Fighting all day long, he oppresses me.

56.4:
In Elohim, whose Word I praise, 
In Elohim I have trusted; 
I do not fear; 
What could flesh do to me?

56.8:
You have counted my wanderings; 
You put my tears into Your pitcher; 
Are they not in Your Book?

56.11:
In Elohim I have trusted; 
I do not fear; 
What could man do to me?

57.3:
He sends from the shamayim and saves me; 
He reproaches the one who would swallow me up. Selah. 
Elohim sends forth His kindness and His truth.

57.6:
They have prepared a net for my footsteps; 
My being was bowed down; 
They have dug a pit before me; 
They fell into the midst of it! Selah.

57.7:
My heart is firm, O Elohim, 
My heart is firm; 
I sing and praise.

57.9:
I praise You among the peoples, 
O Aḏonai; 
I sing to You among the nations.

57.11:
Be exalted above the shamayim, 
O Elohim; 
Let Your esteem be above all the earth.

59.3:
For look, they have lain in wait for my life; 
Mighty men assemble against me, 
For no transgression or sin of mine, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄,

59.11:
Do not slay them, lest my people forget; 
Scatter them by Your power, 
And bring them down, O Aḏonai our shield.

59.16:
And I, I sing of Your power; 
And in the morning I sing aloud of Your kindness; 
For You have been my strong tower 
And a refuge in the day of my distress.

59.17:
O my Strength, to You I sing praises; 
For Elohim is my strong tower, 
My Elohim of kindness.

6.6:
I have grown weary with my groaning; 
Every night I flood my bed; 
I drench my couch with my tears.

60.1:
O Elohim, You have rejected us; 
You have broken us; 
You have been displeased; 
Turn back to us!

60.2:
You have made the earth tremble; 
You have broken it; 
Heal its breaches, for it is shaken.

61.2:
From the end of the earth I call unto You, 
When my heart is faint; 
Lead me to the rock that is higher than I.

61.5:
For You, O Elohim, have heard my vows; 
You have given me the inheritance 
Of those who revere Your Name.

62.4:
They plotted to topple him from his high position; 
They delight in lies; 
They baraḵ with their mouth, 
But in their heart they curse. Selah.

62.8:
Trust in Him at all times, you people; 
Pour out your heart before Him; 
Elohim is a refuge for us. Selah.

63.1:
O Elohim, You are my Ĕl; 
I earnestly seek You; 
My being has thirsted for You; 
My flesh has longed for You 
In a dry and thirsty land without water.

63.10:
They are handed over 
To the power of the sword; 
They become a portion for jackals.

63.11:
But let the meleḵ rejoice in Elohim; 
Let everyone who swears by Him exult; 
For the mouth of those speaking lies are stopped.

64.5:
They arm themselves with an evil word; 
They talk of hiding snares; 
They have said, “Who sees them?”

64.8:
And they cause one to stumble, 
Their own tongue is against them; 
All who see them flee away.

65.3:
Wicked matters were mightier than I; 
As for our transgressions, 
You cover them.

65.8:
And they who dwell in the farthest parts, 
Are afraid of Your signs; 
You make the outgoings of the morning and evening rejoice.

65.9:
You have visited the earth and watered it, 
You greatly enrich it; 
The river of Elohim is filled with water; 
You provide their grain, 
For so You have prepared it.

65.13:
The meadows are dressed in flocks, 
And valleys are covered with grain; 
They shout for joy and sing.

66.7:
Who rules by His power forever; 
His eyes keeping watch on the gentiles; 
Let the rebellious not exalt themselves. Selah.

66.12:
You have let men ride at our head; 
We went through fire and through water; 
But You brought us out to plenty.

66.15:
Burnt offerings of fatlings I offer to You, 
With the incense of rams; 
I offer bulls with goats. Selah.

68.6:
Elohim makes a home for lonely; 
He brings out into prosperity 
Those who are bound with chains; 
Only the rebellious shall dwell in a dry land.

68.23:
“So that you plunge your foot in blood; 
That the tongues of your dogs 
Have their portion from the enemies.”

68.25:
The singers went in front, 
The players on instruments after them; 
Among them were the maidens playing tambourines.

68.34:
Ascribe strength to Elohim; 
His excellence is over Yisra’ĕl, 
And His strength is in the clouds.

69.3:
I am worn out from my crying; 
My throat is dry; 
My eyes grow dim 
As I wait for my Elohim.

69.4:
Those who hate me without a cause 
Are more than the hairs of my head; 
They are mighty who would destroy me, 
My lying enemies; 
What I did not steal, I restored.

69.17:
And do not hide Your face from Your servant, 
For I am in distress; 
Answer me speedily.

69.19:
You Yourself know my reproach, 
And my shame and my confusion; 
My adversaries are all before You.

69.20:
Reproach has broken my heart and I am sick; 
I looked for sympathy, but there was none; 
And for comforters, but I found none.

69.29:
But I am poor and in pain; 
Let Your deliverance, 
O Elohim, place me up on high.

7.8:
𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 judges the peoples; 
Judge me, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, according to my righteousness, 
And according to my integrity within me.

7.9:
Please let the evil of the wicked be ended, 
And establish the righteous; 
For the righteous Elohim is a trier of hearts and kidneys.

70.5:
But I am poor and needy; 
Hasten to me, O Elohim! 
You are my help and my deliverer; 
O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, do not delay.

71.6:
Upon You I have leaned from my birth; 
You took me out of my mother’s womb. 
My praise is continually of You.

72.17:
Let His Name be forever, 
His Name continue before the sun; 
And let them baraḵ themselves in Him; 
Let all nations call Him fortunate.

73.27:
For look, those who are far from You perish; 
You shall cut off all those 
Who go whoring away from You.

74.4:
Your adversaries have roared 
In the midst of Your appointments; 
They have put up their own signs as signs.

76.5:
The stout-hearted have been stripped; 
They slept their sleep; 
And none of the mighty men have found their hands.

76.7:
You, You are to be revered; 
And who would stand in Your presence 
When You are displeased?

77.16:
The waters saw You, O Elohim; 
The waters saw You, they were afraid; 
The depths also trembled.

77.17:
The clouds poured out water; 
The shamayim rumbled; 
Also, Your arrows flashed back and forth.

77.18:
The voice of Your thunder rolled along; 
Lightnings lit up the world; 
The earth trembled and shook.

78.21:
Therefore 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 heard, and He was wroth; 
So a fire was kindled against Ya’aqoḇ, 
And displeasure also came up against Yisra’ĕl,

78.50:
He made a path for His displeasure; 
He did not spare their being from death, 
But gave their life over to the plague.

78.57:
But they turned back 
And acted treacherously like their fathers; 
They twisted like a treacherous bow.

79.1:
A psalm of Asaph. O Elohim, the gentiles have come into Your inheritance; 
They have defiled Your qodesh Hĕyḵal; 
They turned Yerushalayim into ruins.

79.13:
And we, Your people and the sheep of Your pasture, 
We give thanks to You forever; 
From generation to generation we show forth Your praise.

80.1:
Give ear, O Shepherd of Yisra’ĕl, 
Who leads Yosĕph like a flock; 
Who dwells between the keruḇim, shine forth!

80.14:
Return, we beg You, O Elohim of hosts; 
Look down from the shamayim, and see, 
And visit this vine,

81.5:
He appointed it in Yahosĕph for a witness, 
When He went throughout the land of Mitsrayim; 
I heard a language that I did not know.

81.7:
“You called in distress, and I rescued you; 
I answered you in the covering of thunder; 
I proved you at the waters of Meriḇah. Selah.

81.10:
“I am 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 your Elohim, 
Who brought you out of the land of Mitsrayim; 
Open your mouth wide, and I fill it.

83.18:
And let them know that You, 
Whose Name is 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄; 
You alone are the Most High over all the earth.

84.2:
My being has longed, and even fainted, 
For the courts of 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄; 
My heart and my flesh cry out for the living Ĕl.

84.6:
Passing through the valley of weeping, 
They make it a fountain; 
The Teacher also covers it with bireḵoth.

84.11:
For 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 Elohim is a brilliance and a shield; 
𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 gives favor and esteem; 
He withholds no goodness 
From those who walk blamelessly.

86.2:
Guard my being, for I am kindly; 
You are my Elohim; 
Save Your servant who is trusting in You!

86.11:
Teach me Your Way, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄; 
Let me walk in Your truth; 
Unite my heart to revere Your Name.

87.4:
“I mention Rahaḇ and Baḇel to those who know Me; 
See, O Pelesheth and Tsor, with Kush, 
‘This and that one was born there.’ ”

87.5:
And of Tsiyon it is said, 
“Each one was born in her; 
For the Most High Himself establishes her.”

88.8:
You have put away my friends far from me; 
You have made me an abomination to them; 
I am shut in and do not go out;

88.9:
My eye grows dim because of affliction. 
𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, I have called upon You, all day long; 
I have stretched out my hands to You.

88.15:
I am afflicted and dying from childhood; 
I have borne fear from You; 
I am in despair.

89.1:
I sing of the kindnesses of 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 forever; 
With my mouth I make known Your trustworthiness 
To all generations.

89.9:
You rule the swelling of the sea; 
When its waves rise, 
You still them.

89.10:
You have broken Rahaḇ in pieces, as one who is slain; 
You have scattered Your enemies 
With the arm of Your strength.

89.14:
Righteousness and Right-Ruling 
Are the foundation of Your throne; 
Kindness and truth go before Your face.

9.6:
The enemy is no more – ruins everlasting!
And You have uprooted the cities; 
Even their remembrance has perished.

9.19:
Arise, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, 
Do not let man prevail; 
Let the gentiles be judged before Your face.

90.10:
The days of our lives are seventy years; 
Or if due to strength, eighty years, 
Yet the best of them is but toil and exertion; 
For it is soon cut off, and we fly away.

91.4:
He covers you with His feathers, 
And under His wings you take refuge; 
His truth is a shield and armor.

91.7:
A thousand fall at your side, 
And ten thousand at your right hand; 
But it does not come near you.

91.15:
“When he calls on Me, I answer him; 
I am with him in distress; 
I deliver him and esteem him.

92.1:
It is good to give thanks to 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, 
And to sing praises to Your Name, 
O Most High;

92.9:
For look, Your enemies, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, 
For look, Your enemies do perish; 
All the workers of wickedness are scattered.

92.11:
And my eye looks upon my enemies; 
My ears hear the evil-doers 
Who rise up against me.

93.1:
𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 shall reign, 
He shall put on excellency; 
𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 shall put on strength; 
He shall gird Himself. 
Indeed, the world is established, immovable.

93.3:
Rivers shall lift up, O 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄, 
Rivers shall lift up their voice; 
Rivers lift up their breakers.

94.4:
They pour forth, 
They speak arrogantly; 
All the workers of wickedness boast in themselves.

94.23:
And brings back on them their own wickedness, 
And cuts them off in their own wickedness; 
𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 our Elohim cuts them off.

99.1:
𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 shall reign; 
Peoples tremble! 
He is enthroned on the keruḇim; 
The earth shakes!

99.4:
And the strength of the Meleḵ. 
Shall love Right-Ruling; 
You Yourself shall establish straightness; 
You shall execute right-ruling 
And righteousness in Ya’aqoḇ.

99.7:
He spoke to them in the column of cloud; 
They guarded His Witnesses 
And the Law He gave them.

99.9:
Exalt 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 our Elohim, 
And bow down towards His qodesh mountain; 
For 𐤉𐤄𐤅𐤄 our Elohim is qodesh.
